        <!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
        <div id="exec-summary" class="nav-section active">
            <div class="section">
                <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
                <p>This report analyzes the global frozen yogurt and frozen custard categories to determine which concept offers the strongest opportunity for a premium frozen dessert brand entering Casablanca, Morocco.</p>
                
                <h3>What We Know</h3>
                <p><strong>Global market maturity:</strong> Frozen yogurt is the larger, more mature category (~$3–9B globally); frozen custard is smaller but concentrated (~$1.4B), primarily in North America. Frozen yogurt dominates Asia-Pacific; frozen custard is Midwest USA/North America-centric.</p>
                
                <p><strong>Consumer sentiment:</strong> Frozen yogurt appeals to health-conscious consumers (probiotics, lower fat) and Gen Z (customization, social media). Frozen custard builds fierce loyalty (nostalgia, richness, premium perception, daily-fresh positioning). Both support premium pricing.</p>

                <div class="key-finding">
                    <strong>Critical Market Gap:</strong> No significant established frozen-custard category exists in Morocco, while frozen yogurt has minimal presence. This represents both opportunity and risk — low category awareness vs. low competition.
                </div>

                <h3>Comparative Strengths</h3>
                <div class="comparison-row">
                    <div class="comparison-item frozen-yogurt">
                        <strong>Frozen Yogurt</strong>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Global consumer familiarity</li>
                            <li>Strong customization appeal</li>
                            <li>Health perception (lower entry barrier)</li>
                            <li>Proven playbook (Pinkberry, Yogurtland)</li>
                            <li>High Instagram/TikTok potential</li>
                            <li>Lower risk, established category</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="comparison-item frozen-custard">
                        <strong>Frozen Custard</strong>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Extremely high product differentiation</li>
                            <li>Premium perception (egg yolks, richness)</li>
                            <li>Exceptional brand loyalty (Culver's 40-yr data)</li>
                            <li>Limited competition in Morocco</li>
                            <li>Strong repeat-purchase drivers</li>
                            <li>Category creation advantage</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3>Risk Profile</h3>
                <div class="comparison-row">
                    <div class="comparison-item frozen-yogurt">
                        <strong>Risks</strong>
                        <ul>
                            <li>High fragmentation; hard to stand out</li>
                            <li>Lower perceived differentiation</li>
                            <li>Customization alone ≠ brand loyalty</li>
                            <li>Perception challenged by toppings nutrition</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="comparison-item frozen-custard">
                        <strong>Risks</strong>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Consumer education required</li>
                            <li>Higher execution bar (fresh daily)</li>
                            <li>Market unproven in Morocco</li>
                            <li>Richer product may reduce frequency for some</li>
                            <li>Import dependencies (dairy sourcing)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3>Preliminary Verdict</h3>
                <p><strong>Frozen Yogurt:</strong> Lower-risk, proven, customizable. Works. But enters a crowded category globally; will compete on execution and brand, not novelty.</p>
                <p><strong>Frozen Custard:</strong> Higher-risk, highly differentiated, defensible. Category ownership possible. Loyalty data from Culver's (40+ years, $4.2M AUV) suggests deep consumer appeal once established.</p>

                <div class="decision-frame">
                    <h4>Hypothesis to Validate</h4>
                    <p><strong>Frozen Yogurt</strong> = lower-risk, easier-to-understand, highly customizable entry strategy for a broader market.</p>
                    <p><strong>Frozen Custard</strong> = higher-risk but potentially much more differentiated, premium, and defensible in Morocco.</p>
                    <p>The evidence below will test which aligns with your brand vision.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

