                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Brand loyalty</strong></td>
                        <td>Moderate (attached to flavor/toppings, not brand)</td>
                        <td><span class="score-high">High</span> (attached to product & experience)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Social media potential</strong></td>
                        <td><span class="score-high">High</span> (self-serve = endless combinations)</td>
                        <td>Moderate (concretes are visual, less UGC-friendly than froyo)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Family appeal</strong></td>
                        <td><span class="score-high">High</span> (fun, customizable, perceived healthy)</td>
                        <td><span class="score-high">High</span> (bundled with burgers, nostalgic)</td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

                <div class="key-finding">
                    <strong>Business model insight:</strong> Frozen yogurt prioritizes scalability and social virality; frozen custard prioritizes differentiation and loyalty. Yogurt is a distribution play (100s of locations, self-serve efficiency). Custard is a brand play (tight franchisee control, product quality).
